From: Andrzej Rogozynski <sellen@cs-lab.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] Linux console frame buffer and keyboard

Video (i_video_fbdev.c):
- mmap the frame buffer and draw into the visible area (the console
  pans the display), centred; -scaling N (default 1: a 320x200
  window), 8 bpp through the hardware palette (FBIOPUTCMAP), 16/32 bpp
  through a lookup table; lines are copied with move16 on 68040/68060.
- -mode WxH switches to one of the driver's modes (by name, through
  /sys/class/graphics/fb0/mode, so the driver supplies the timings)
  and scales to fit; the console's mode, palette and KD_TEXT are
  restored at exit and on fatal signals.
- the tty is switched to KD_GRAPHICS so fbcon stays off the screen.

Keyboard (i_input_tty.c):
- KDGKBTYPE stores one byte; reading it into an int failed the
  keyboard check on big-endian machines.
- amikbd reports raw Amiga scancodes as keycodes (the console keymap is
  remapped at boot): use an Amiga table when an amiga-keyboard input
  device exists, -pckeys for the PC table.
- kbd_restore() puts the keyboard mode and termios back (called from the
  video cleanup too); Backspace no longer quits the game.

I_Error (i_system.c) ended in an endless loop instead of exiting (and
-timedemo reports its result through I_Error).

